It was dark. The light was only in one of the rooms on the second floor. You silently approached the door. It was not locked. You decisively entered the room.
"Oh, I didn't expect to see you here," said the impudent, "didn't expect you'd guess."
"Why did you put a spell on me?" you severely asked.
"To be honest, there were no specific reason. I just found a new interesting spell and decided to test it on someone. And you deliberately put that skin on yourself. It would be a damn shame not to use a chance!"
You was shocked by the cruelty of this person and the senselessness of what was going on.
"Break the spell," you finally said. 
"No," he said by an indifferent tone.
You felt like someone whipped you. You swiftly attacked the enemy and bit his arm.
"What have you done?!" he screamed with despair.
"Break the spell," you repeated the demand, "so you will also be cured."
By shaking hands he opened some old book and quickly red the necessary passage. After giving this pathetic person a disdainful look, you left. Soon you returned to your normal life, and those few days as a wolf, you tried to forget like a mere nightmare.